{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["<b>By lot shall his inheritance be divided.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted this in light of what Scripture says (Proverbs 18:18): ״מדינים ישבית הגורל ובין עצומים יפריד״ — 'The lot puts an end to contentions, and separates among the mighty.' This comes to praise the division by lot, for it is an esteemed measure for dividing, because it silences contentions and is a cause for preventing desire — so that no person will henceforth covet his fellow's portion, since it came to him by lot; rather, he will say, 'it was his from HaShem.' As it is written (ibid. 16): ״בחיק יוטל את הגורל ומה' כל משפטו״ — 'The lot is cast into the lap, and its every decision is from HaShem.' 'And separates among the mighty' — among the divisions and quarrels, in the language of (Isaiah 41): ״הגישו עצומותיכם״ — 'bring forward your mighty ones.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:17.586467938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}